## Key Learnings & Notes:
- **Expo Go Compatibility**: Must use mock Firebase for testing (real Firebase requires dev build)
- **Import Consistency**: Always import auth functions from same source as auth object
- **Mock Limitations**: User data resets on app reload (expected for mock)
- **Phase 2 Success**: Friend system fully functional with mock Firestore
- **Navigation Focus**: Use focus listeners to refresh data when returning to screens
- **Mock Data Structure**: Create realistic test data with interconnected relationships
- **Phase 3 Success**: Ephemeral posts fully functional with mock storage and Firestore
- **Image Handling**: Mock storage returns placeholder URLs; real storage will return actual media
- **Expo Camera Alternative**: expo-image-picker works in Expo Go as camera replacement
- **Delete-on-View**: Successfully implemented with proper view tracking
- **Feed Visibility**: Complex filtering respects friend relationships and privacy settings
- **Phase 4 Success**: Direct messaging fully functional with ephemeral features
- **React Native Paper**: Must wrap app with PaperProvider for Paper components to work
- **MVP Core Complete**: All major features implemented and tested successfully